SUMMARY:University Statistics
DESCRIPTION:Overview Al-Qadisiyah University was founded in 1987 and is today one of Iraq&rsquo;s leading public universities. This page presents cumulative and annual statistics, updated yearly.\nKey Figures Indicator Count Colleges 18 Academic Departments ~110 Research Centres 4 main centres Faculty Members ~2,400 (professors, lecturers, assistant lecturers, instructors) Enrolled Students ~35,000 (undergraduate + postgraduate) Administrative Staff ~1,800 Scientific Publications (Scopus, cumulative) Updated annually — see Research Statistics Patents Updated annually — see Patents Editor note: Refresh the numbers above annually from the deanship and statistics office reports. Last updated: TODO.\nCumulative Trend Academic Year Students Faculty Publications 2024–2025 TODO TODO TODO 2023–2024 TODO TODO TODO 2022–2023 TODO TODO TODO Distribution by Programme Level Undergraduate (Bachelor&rsquo;s): ~80% of students Postgraduate (Master&rsquo;s &amp; PhD): ~20% of students Alumni Since founding, more than 100,000 students have graduated from Al-Qadisiyah University and now work across public and private sectors in Iraq and abroad. See the Alumni gateway.\nSee Also Detailed Research Statistics Administrative Statistics Global Rankings 
